  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nX : Y = 3 : 2\n\nInitial X = ₹30,000\n\nTotal profit = ₹186,000 (for 12 months)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nCapital-time = Capital × Time (months)\n\nProfit share ∝ Capital-time\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n⇒ Y initial = (2/3) × 30,000 = ₹20,000\n\n⇒ X: 30,000 for 4 months ⇒ 30,000 × 4 = 120,000\n\n⇒ X: 40,000 for 8 months (after adding 10,000) ⇒ 40,000 × 8 = 320,000\n\n⇒ X total = 120,000 + 320,000 = 440,000\n\n⇒ Y: 20,000 for 6 months ⇒ 20,000 × 6 = 120,000\n\n⇒ Y: 10,000 for 6 months (after halving) ⇒ 10,000 × 6 = 60,000\n\n⇒ Y total = 120,000 + 60,000 = 180,000\n\n⇒ Ratio X : Y = 440,000 : 180,000 = 22 : 9\n\n⇒ Y's fraction = 9 / (22 + 9) = 9 / 31\n\n⇒ Y's profit = 186,000 × (9/31) = (186,000 ÷ 31) × 9 = 6,000 × 9 = ₹54,000\n\n**∴ Y’s profit = ₹54,000.**\n\n39:T9d7,",
